# Shell preferences

- **Bash over PowerShell:** The maintainer uses Git Bash on Windows. Always propose Bash commands and scripts (e.g. `./scripts/foo.sh`), never PowerShell. Git Bash is installed with Git and is the preferred shell for this project.
- **On Windows, avoid bare `bash` when launching from another shell:** `bash` may resolve to `C:\Windows\System32\bash.exe` (WSL) instead of Git Bash. When you need Bash from a Windows-hosted shell, prefer the explicit Git Bash path `C:\Program Files\Git\bin\bash.exe` or a repo wrapper that uses it.
